course: dictionary
lesson: 16014
title: The vastness of space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Vastness is a noun. It means how extremely large, wide or huge something is. It can also name a very large, empty place, such as a desert, an ocean or space. «Sam looked up at the night sky and felt the vastness of space.» The sky is huge and empty, so vastness means its great size.
explain: Writers use vastness to help you feel how big something is. «Out in the desert, the vastness of the sand stretched on for miles.» Miles of sand with nothing else in sight make you feel small. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Vastness often makes a person feel small or lonely. «In the vastness of the ocean, the little boat looked like a speck.» The boat is tiny next to the sea. Look for clues such as space, ocean, desert and sea near the word: they show you what is so big.
fact: Vastness is a noun, so you can say «the vastness of the sea».
fact: «Vastness» means being extremely large, wide or huge.
fact: «Vastness» can also mean a very large, empty area, such as a desert, an ocean or space.
fact: Phrases to spot are «the vastness of space» and «in the vastness of».
fact: Writers use vastness to make readers feel small or lonely.
exercise: «The stars shone over the vastness of the desert.» What does vastness mean here? | A loud noise | *A very large, empty area | A bright light | Cosy little room
exercise: «The sailors felt small in the vastness of the ocean.» Why did they feel small? | They were sleeping | The ocean was tiny | They were tired from rowing | *The sea was huge and went on for miles
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the big empty place: «Lila gazed into the vastness of space.» | gazed | *space | into | Lila
test: «The vastness of the ocean made the little fishing boat look tiny.» What does vastness mean? | *The great size of the sea | A loud storm | A small fish | A sandy beach
test: Which phrase uses vastness correctly? | the vastness of a cup of tea | *the vastness of space | the vastness of a pencil | the vastness of my lunch box
exam: «Standing on the cliff, Ben felt lonely in the vastness of the empty sea.» What feeling does vastness help show? | Fear of the dark | Feeling hungry and tired | *Feeling small and lonely | Feeling very loud and happy
